.TH "OSTRYA\-SHOW" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-show \- Print the report of an object, or one part of its commit metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya show [OPTIONS] [OBJECT]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the report of an object, or one part of its commit metadata.
.PP
For a commit, a dirtree, or a dirmeta, the command prints the object type and the checksum. A commit then gets its report: the parent, the content checksum, the date in UTC, the \fB\%version\fR metadata key if present, the subject, and the body. The GPG signatures of the commit follow, if it has any. For a file object, the command prints its header: the file type, the size or the symlink target, the mode, the owner, and the extended attributes.
.PP
The report options exclude each other. If the command line holds more than one, the first in this order wins: \%\-\-print\-detached\-metadata\-key, \%\-\-print\-metadata\-key, \%\-\-list\-detached\-metadata\-keys, \%\-\-list\-metadata\-keys, \%\-\-print\-related, \%\-\-print\-variant\-type, and \%\-\-print\-sizes.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIOBJECT\fR
The object to report: a revision or an object checksum. Required.
.IP
A full checksum can name a metadata object or a file object. The command looks for a commit, a dirtree, a dirmeta, and a file object, in that order. With \%\-\-print\-variant\-type, OBJECT is a file name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-related\fR
Show the \%"related" commits.
.IP
The command prints one \fB\%<name> <checksum>\fR line for each dependency of the commit, the entries of field \%2 of the commit object, in the stored order. An empty field prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-variant\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
Read OBJECT as a file that holds a value of this GVariant type.
.IP
The command prints the value in the GVariant text form, with the byte order of its numbers converted. \%\-B has no effect here. The command refuses a file larger than \%16 MiB.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-metadata\-keys\fR
List the metadata keys of the commit, one on each line, sorted.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-metadata\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR
Print the value of one metadata key.
.IP
The value prints in the GVariant text form. A key that the commit metadata does not hold is an error.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-hex\fR
Print a \%byte\-array key value as an unquoted hexadecimal string.
.IP
This switch applies to \%\-\-print\-metadata\-key and \%\-\-print\-detached\-metadata\-key. The hex digits are lowercase. A value of another type ignores the switch.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-detached\-metadata\-keys\fR
List the detached metadata keys of the commit, one on each line, sorted.
.IP
A commit with no detached metadata is an error.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-detached\-metadata\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR
Print the value of one detached metadata key.
.IP
The value prints in the GVariant text form. A commit with no detached metadata is an error, and so is a key that it does not hold.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-sizes\fR
Print the sizes that the \fB\%ostree.sizes\fR metadata of the commit records.
.IP
The command prints the compressed size, the unpacked size, and the object count. Each is a \%needed/total pair. The needed values cover the objects that the local store does not hold. A commit with no \fB\%ostree.sizes\fR key is an error.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
Show the raw variant data.
.IP
The command prints the value of the object in the GVariant text form, after the type line. For a commit, the commit report does not follow. For a file object, this switch has no effect.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-no\-byteswap\fR
Do not convert the variant data from big endian.
.IP
The command prints the raw variant as stored. For a commit, the report of the commit follows it, also with \%\-\-raw. The switch also applies to the values of \%\-\-print\-metadata\-key and \%\-\-print\-detached\-metadata\-key.
.TP
\fB\-\-gpg\-homedir\fR \fIHOMEDIR\fR
The GPG home directory that holds the keyrings.
.IP
The command reads each \fB\%*.gpg\fR file in HOMEDIR as a keyring, together with the \fB\%gpgkeys.gpg\fR file of the repository. It uses these keyrings to verify the GPG signatures in the commit report. \%\-\-gpg\-verify\-remote wins over this option.
.TP
\fB\-\-gpg\-verify\-remote\fR \fIREMOTE\fR
Use the GPG configuration of this remote to verify signatures.
.IP
The keyrings are \fB\%<remote>.trustedkeys.gpg\fR in the repository and in \fB\%/etc/ostree/remotes.d/\fR, and the global trusted keyrings. The global keyrings are the \fB\%*.gpg\fR files in the directory that \fB\%OSTREE_GPG_HOME\fR names, or in \fB\%/usr/share/ostree/trusted.gpg.d/\fR\&.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
